    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Reserve Bank of India was established on April 1, 1935, under the provisions of the Reserve Bank of India Act, 1934.",
        "The institution was created following the recommendations of the Royal Commission on Indian Currency and Finance (Hilton Young Commission, 1926).",
        "Originally established as a private shareholders' bank with a capital of Rs. 5 crore, it was fully nationalized on January 1, 1949.",
        "The Central Office was initially established in Kolkata and was permanently relocated to Mumbai in 1937."
      ],
      "id": "m7dse15"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Note the nationalization date: RBI was nationalized on January 1, 1949, under the RBI (Transfer to Public Ownership) Act, 1948.",
        "Commission history: Remember that the Hilton Young Commission (1926) recommended setting up the central bank.",
        "Headquarters shift: Central office shifted from Kolkata to Mumbai in 1937."
      ],
